A||||3||PAUL88GT||How to remove inside door handle?||||1||
Z||000000||PAUL88GT||04-26-2001||06:11 PM||||My inside door handle is broken in the rear where it attaches to the latch rod.<P>I have the inner door panel off.  Do I remove the pin with spring?  <P>I am having trouble getting the pin removed. I cannot seem to get the tabs small enough to get pin to back out so I am not sure if this is the correct way to remove the handle.  Another way would be to cut the pin.<BR>It also looks like the rivet on the handle frame in the door could be drilled out.<P>Any suggestions?<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-26-2001||06:17 PM||||Drill out the rivit and install a different assy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||04-27-2001||11:11 AM||||Indiana:<P>Thanks for the response.  Should I use a large sheet metal screw or bolt with nut when I reinstall the new assembly?<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-27-2001||12:08 PM||||If your not going to rivet, use a short carriage bolt-head toward the inside of car-nut inside. Trim it to length if too long and use some locktite on the threads.||||reg||1
